# Shell scripts must keep LF endings, whatever the checkout platform.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true a Windows working tree gets CRLF, and a script copied
# from there to Linux has a shebang reading `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` — the shell
# looks for an interpreter literally named "bash\r" and reports command not
# found, which sends you looking for a missing file that is right there.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by tools on the engagement box.
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
